WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.119
One coding agent is
easy to keep an eye on.

2
00:00:04.169 --> 00:00:08.013
Run four at once, and you lose
track of which one needs you.

3
00:00:08.513 --> 00:00:13.436
Irie runs your AI coding agents
side by side, in one calm view.

4
00:00:13.486 --> 00:00:19.198
Type a task, and it gets its own card,
its own terminal and its own git worktree.

5
00:00:19.898 --> 00:00:23.135
When an agent needs you,
its card turns red.

6
00:00:23.185 --> 00:00:26.755
Answer it in its terminal,
and it goes back to work.

7
00:00:26.855 --> 00:00:28.504
The rest stay calm.

8
00:00:29.204 --> 00:00:32.446
Your agents run in tmux,
not in the window.

9
00:00:32.496 --> 00:00:35.146
Close the window, and they keep working.

10
00:00:35.246 --> 00:00:37.906
Open it again, and nothing has stopped.

11
00:00:38.606 --> 00:00:41.861
Send small jobs to a
model on your own machine.

12
00:00:41.911 --> 00:00:44.012
It costs nothing per token.

13
00:00:44.062 --> 00:00:46.888
Keep the strongest
model for the hard ones.

14
00:00:46.938 --> 00:00:50.347
Irie works with any agent
that runs in a terminal,

15
00:00:50.387 --> 00:00:53.157
with the deepest support for Claude Code.

16
00:00:54.057 --> 00:00:57.745
Irie has no server,
no account and no telemetry.

17
00:00:57.845 --> 00:01:01.669
It's free and open source,
with no company behind it.

18
00:01:01.769 --> 00:01:05.236
One line installs it,
on a Mac or on Linux.

19
00:01:05.536 --> 00:01:07.027
Everything irie.
